From 8644304094e77b22a05d325d7fa4ae709f6d883b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:30:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 73/74] media: qcom: camss: C-PHY on SM8450/SM8475 (CSIPHY
 v2.1.3)

On top of the C-PHY support from the Xiaomi Mi 10T (SM8250) port:

 - the v2.1.3 three-phase lane sequence (28 registers per trio) and the
   rate dependent settings for 1.7, 2.1 and 2.5 Gsym/s per trio, from
   the vendor camera-kernel tables (cam_csiphy_2_1_3_hwreg.h, the
   standard table that the diting "qcom,csiphy-v2.1.3" DT selects)
 - the v2.1.3 common block: CTRL7 0x7a and CTRL33 cleared before the
   trios, the three-phase reset exit value 0x0e in CTRL0 after them
 - PHY type C-PHY in CSID 680's CSI2_RX_CFG0
 - the rate bucket is chosen on the symbol rate, twice the V4L2 link
   frequency (pixel rate = link_freq * 2 * trios * 16 / 7 / bpp); the
   SM8250 port took the link frequency for the symbol rate, which made
   no difference with its single bucket

The settle count stays the SM8250 dump value (0x1d).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
